# Godot: Prewired Scene Nodes Only

When a node already exists in the scene, wire it once in the scene script with `@onready` and use that member directly.

## Do

- Define scene-node members at the top of the owning script:
  - `@onready var button: Button = $Control/Button`
  - `@onready var selection_circle: TextureRect = $Control/VBoxContainer/CharacterSprite/SelectionCircle`
- Keep node ownership local: the scene script that owns the node handles its own button signal wiring.
- Expose typed signals from the owner script for outside systems (`target_pressed`, `target_hover_entered`, etc.).

## Do Not

- Do runtime path lookups in gameplay wiring for nodes that already exist in the scene tree.
- Reconstruct or re-fetch child-node references in other scripts when an owning script already has `@onready` refs.
- Add wrapper "safety" fallbacks for missing required scene nodes; missing nodes should fail loudly in dev.
